WEBVTT

00:00:00.058 --> 00:00:01.196
Here's what happens when you ask

00:00:01.196 --> 00:00:02.508
Claude for a video.

00:00:02.508 --> 00:00:03.831
First, you describe it,

00:00:03.831 --> 00:00:04.981
in plain words.

00:00:04.981 --> 00:00:07.210
Claude turns that into a plan:

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.509
what's said, and what's on screen.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.668
Then it gathers the pieces.

00:00:11.668 --> 00:00:13.282
A voice from ElevenLabs.

00:00:13.282 --> 00:00:14.698
Footage from Pexels.

00:00:14.698 --> 00:00:16.347
Art from Gemini.

00:00:16.347 --> 00:00:17.589
Every frame is drawn like

00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:18.460
a web page,

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:19.888
one at a time.

00:00:19.888 --> 00:00:21.339
And before anything renders,

00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:22.686
Claude shows you a preview,

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:23.824
so you can say:

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:25.647
make that title bigger.

00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:28.143
Then ffmpeg stitches the frames

00:00:28.143 --> 00:00:30.221
and the sound into a video.

00:00:30.221 --> 00:00:31.568
Your notes go in.

00:00:31.568 --> 00:00:33.696
A finished video comes out.
